{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Cribl decrypt panel\nPut one or more Cribl `#keyId:iv:ct#` tokens (space- or comma-separated) in **Tokens**, set **FunctionEndpoint** to your decrypt Function URL (including `?code=`), and the grid below shows the decrypted plaintext.\n\nKQL can't AES-decrypt inline, so this calls the Azure Function (which holds no keys itself \u2014 it pulls them from Key Vault) and renders the result. _POC note: the function key is a secret; prefer a per-user prompt over saving it in the workbook._"
      },
      "name": "intro"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "p-endpoint",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "FunctionEndpoint",
            "label": "Function endpoint (incl. ?code=)",
            "type": 1,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "https://cribldec-func-ukz4eyn7t4iik.azurewebsites.net/api/decrypt?code=PASTE_FUNCTION_KEY"
          },
          {
            "id": "p-tokens",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "Tokens",
            "label": "Tokens (space/comma-separated)",
            "type": 1,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "#TWPLRh::2B0RXsyqPFimLaEjyjZx8ga/XOpXn+HIDVnbKOigKwg# #tqVVX3:lp21TwfoZOew4X+QQ/6Lbw:Q6E40/+W1SqKZv7PiALmNXXrZROzqi/jaTYwCD5/HA8#"
          }
        ],
        "style": "above",
        "queryType": 0
      },
      "name": "parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "{\"version\": \"CustomEndpoint/1.0\", \"data\": null, \"headers\": [{\"name\": \"Content-Type\", \"value\": \"application/json\"}], \"method\": \"POST\", \"url\": \"{FunctionEndpoint}\", \"body\": \"{\\\"tokens\\\": \\\"{Tokens}\\\"}\", \"transformers\": [{\"type\": \"jsonpath\", \"settings\": {\"tablePath\": \"$.results\", \"columns\": [{\"path\": \"$.input\", \"columnid\": \"Token\"}, {\"path\": \"$.plaintext\", \"columnid\": \"Plaintext\"}, {\"path\": \"$.ok\", \"columnid\": \"OK\"}, {\"path\": \"$.error\", \"columnid\": \"Error\"}]}}]}",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Decrypted values",
        "queryType": 10,
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "OK",
              "formatter": 18,
              "formatOptions": {
                "thresholdsOptions": "icons",
                "thresholdsGrid": [
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "true",
                    "representation": "success",
                    "text": ""
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "Default",
                    "thresholdValue": null,
                    "representation": "error",
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "decrypt-grid"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### Feeding from a table (production)\nDrive **Tokens** from a parameter query over your ingested data:\n\n```kql\nMyCriblTable_CL\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)\n| summarize Tokens = strcat_array(make_list(EncryptedField_s), ' ')\n```\nSet that query as the source for the `Tokens` parameter, then this panel decrypts the column."
      },
      "name": "prod-note"
    }
  ],
  "$schema": "https://github.com/Microsoft/Application-Insights-Workbooks/blob/master/schema/workbook.json"
}